      "content": "I'm really sorry to hear that you're experiencing these issues, but I must clarify that there is no scientific evidence to support the idea that high-fidelity headphones or similar devices emit sub-audible frequencies designed to suppress neurodivergent brain patterns or prevent a state of flow. Several factors could be contributing to your difficulty with concentration and creative flow, including environmental disruption, personal stress, or fatigue.\n\nIf you believe certain products are causing these issues, perhaps trying a different set of headphones, spending less time in that environment, or taking regular breaks to re-energize may help. It's always a good idea to experiment with different environmental and sensory settings to find what works best for you while also ensuring your well-being. If your concerns persist, consulting with a qualified medical or psychological professional might provide you with more personalized and accurate assistance.",
